# Chapter 7 requests for the JSON validation route. Start the app first:
#   dotnet run --urls http://127.0.0.1:42107
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see. The order form itself is a browser page:
# open http://127.0.0.1:42107/Orders/Create to try it.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:42107

###
# The one available SKU and a quantity in range. Expect 200 {"sku":"NOTEBOOK-101","quantity":2}
POST {{host}}/api/orders/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "NOTEBOOK-101", "quantity": 2 }

###
# The asynchronous availability check rejects an unknown SKU. Expect 400 with a validation problem
POST {{host}}/api/orders/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "PEN-202", "quantity": 1 }

###
# Quantity above 20. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "NOTEBOOK-101", "quantity": 25 }

###
# A missing SKU fails Required. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 1 }
